I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services like VirusTotal. However, I can show you what a typical request would look like and give you an example of the kind of response you’d receive.

---

### Example API Request

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/ip_addresses/203.0.113.0/comments?limit=25&cursor=nop
Authorization: Bearer GHI654
Accept: application/json
```

### Example JSON Response

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "comment_1",
      "type": "comments",
      "attributes": {
        "date": "2024-04-01T12:34:56Z",
        "user": "analyst123",
        "text": "Observed malicious activity from this IP."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "comment_2",
      "type": "comments",
      "attributes": {
        "date": "2024-04-02T08:15:30Z",
        "user": "security_bot",
        "text": "IP flagged as part of a botnet."
      }
    }
    // ... up to 25 comments
  ],
  "links": {
    "self": "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/ip_addresses/203.0.113.0/comments?limit=25&cursor=nop",
    "next": "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/ip_addresses/203.0.113.0/comments?limit=25&cursor=abc123"
  },
  "meta": {
    "pagination": {
      "total": 100,
      "limit": 25,
      "cursor": "nop"
    }
  }
}
```

---

If you actually need the real data, you’ll have to run the request yourself (or let me know if you’d like help crafting a script to do it). Let me know how else I can assist!
